#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:7
#: ea4047748389416a8bba4d4c143eab3d
msgid "Using a Vicon indoor positioning system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:9
#: cffeb78241b446ee865027cbe5d6d9d4
msgid "Robotics labs commonly have an indoor flying facility using a Vicon indoor positioning system. These systems use infra-red cameras to give a high rate (200Hz) position and attitude via a network connection. ArduPilot can use this positioning information for precise indoor flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:19
#: 5aa14f9834c243239474273163c6dfbd
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:21
#: df75990b436d442da3189ad126a60636
msgid "The Vicon system comes with a SDK that provides APIs for accessing the Vicon positioning data. To use the Vicon data with ArduPilot you need a tool which can use this API and map it onto MAVLink packets to send to ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:26
#: 59b661d7acff4f42894918b0414882a6
msgid "There are two types of MAVLink packets that can be used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:28
#: 6c31013af4814ac6bf9a79bfd28fde1b
msgid "the GLOBAL_VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE packet, which provides position (NED) and attitude (euler angles)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:31
#: 802e960afa9249b2ba37b2cccbcec491
msgid "the GPS_INPUT packet which provides position as latitude/longitude, altitude, velocity (3D) and yaw data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:34
#: 9e4225e877b842dba966e0771a45edb4
msgid "Right now the best approach is to use GPS_INPUT with the GPS yaw extension as the velocity data provided by the GPS packet is more valuable for good positioning than the attitude information in the GLOBAL_VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE packet. In the future we will support a combined VISION MAVLink message which will provide position, velocity and attitude in one packet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:42
#: 538267413e934be79428758b64cd11cf
msgid "Hardware Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:44
#: eafd6b00c1bc44d89c40ad314466312d
msgid "You will need a low-latency network link from your GCS computer to the copter, and from the GCS to your Vicon server. The recommended method is to use ethernet to the Vicon server and use a ESP8266 WiFi link running :ref:`mavest8266 <common-esp8266-telemetry>` on the copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:50
#: de6a98bc1a4c4d5499d7286b584e5931
msgid "Vicon System Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:52
#: 036d59f23ea747488c58efa89ecd64c5
msgid "The Vicon system should be correctly calibrated. The origin should be set using the calibration wand. In the Vicon Tracker software, the Z-axis (shown in blue) of the Vicon system world frame should point up. We will call the X-axis (red) as North, and the Y-axis (green) as West."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:53
#: da1342d90bfc41e9971ceddeb65cf160
msgid "The UAV should have a minimum of 4 reflective markers to ensure an accurate fix. Any reflective surfaces on the UAV should be covered with masking tape to avoid spurious detections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:54
#: 9aefc57655084fa5ab9efc711fb59561
msgid "Place the UAV in the Vicon space so that the forward direction of the autopilot is facing 'North'. (Figure 1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:55
#: 49261d96158d4cf0b2efa35c46208458
msgid "In the Vicon Tracker, select all of the markers and create a new object for the UAV. The coordinate frame of the UAV should then be aligned with the Vicon world frame, so that X is forward, Y is Left and Z is up. (Figure 2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:60
#: c346925ab09b40edb9434bbf5482b7a7
msgid "Figure 1: Example of how UAV should be positioned when creating the Vicon Object. The forward direction is aligned with the X-axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:65
#: 17732b533b684e36a4898fd2031abb55
msgid "Figure 2: Screenshot from Vicon Tracker software, showing world coordinate frame (bottom left) aligned with UAV coordinate frame. The origin of the object frame should be approximately where the autopilot is located."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:70
#: fd7b44e73c954f18be31fb76ed379317
msgid "These coordinate frame conventions apply to MAVProxy version 1.8.36 and above. Ensure you are using an up-to-date version."
msgstr ""

