msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:191
#: f163b2448b3b4e94b0e018b5146e6ccd
msgid "Checking Orientations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:193
#: ba238569aaff4edc92d3a62d0ae249a0
msgid "Use the Vicon status line in the MAVProxy console to check that you have the right orientation in the data coming from the Vicon. The VPos data is in NED format in meters. The VATT data is euler angles of roll, pitch yaw. Carefully check that these values are consistent while you rotate and move the vehicle before proceeding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:200
#: 50d395e593f5474e9cf29efeb59373aa
msgid "Test Flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:202
#: 3debc61d5c994b6ba4907c95a64e2511
msgid "You should see ArduPilot first report that EKF3 gets yaw alignment, and then that it is using the GPS. After that you should be able to arm and fly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:206
#: 8d09c1cdc3514e44b66a53b817d09a82
msgid "For a first test flight :ref:`Stabilize mode <stabilize-mode>` or :ref:`Alt Hold mode <altholdmode>` mode is recommended. Then get the flight log from the microSD card and check that the EKF3 innovations are low. The position, velocity and yaw normalised innovations should all be low (below 0.1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:211
#: 1b1d475b177f4843a38cb7d651fd5b53
msgid "Once you have confirmed low innovations you can try a flight in :ref:`Loiter mode <loiter-mode>` mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:215
#: ed084237013b40a7a8be8801a64994f0
msgid "Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:217
#: 81627d2bb5384f47a12707ed3aab3aef
msgid "If you have significant vibration then you will likely want to de-weight the accelerometers and instead tell the EKF to use the vicon data more. Try setting :ref:`EK3_ACC_P_NSE <EK3_ACC_P_NSE>` to 2.0 to de-weight the accelerometer data. You may find this helps with position and height hold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:223
#: 572f6d0f08024c4393365a9466bbaa84
msgid "For indoor flight with a Vicon setup and a small quad you can push up the accelerations and yaw rate to much higher value than are used in a normal quad. Some suggestions for a small racing quad are:"
msgstr ""

